# BA_AI_SDLC v2.3.0 GOLD — Universal AI Agent Rules (`.rules`)
# Enforcing the Zero-Bloat & Zero-Gap Constitution Across Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Copilot & Antigravity

## 1. Command Dispatcher & Deterministic CLI Wiring (`@ba-*` <-> `bin/ba-hub.js`)
- `@ba-intake [mode]` -> `workflows/00-ba-intake-router.md` -> Run `npm run hub:intake -- --hub=<hubDir> [--mode=auto|greenfield-brd|high-level|prototype-code|markdown-import|brownfield-cr] [--source=<path>] [--bundle=<json>] [--sprint=<ID>] [--features=<IDs>] [--cr=<CR-ID>]` (`~/` paths auto-expand) to normalize any starting point (`UX_DESIGN_BRIEF.md` for `high-level`/`prototype-code`, lossless `.md` import, or `PARTIAL_JIT_ANCHOR` `As-Is v1.0.0` anchors for `brownfield-cr`).
- `@ba-bootstrap` -> `workflows/01-ba-bootstrap.md` -> Run `npm run hub:init -- --target=<hubDir> --project=<CODE> --name="<Name>"`, present Pass 1 Kickoff Table (`Option A` defaults, max 5 questions), emit `v1.0.0` `00-project-core/` & `01-roadmap-and-pm/`, and verify with `npm run hub:verify -- --hub=<hubDir> --strict`.
- `@ba-sprint-plan [Scope]` -> `workflows/02-ba-sprint-plan.md` -> Allocate `02-sprints/<SprintID>/`, `Wave 1..3` order, `SUP-*` enablers, and mandatory Feature Archetypes (`READ_VIEW` | `MUTATION_WORKFLOW` | `INTEGRATION_JOB`).
- `@ba-sprint-batch [SprintID]` -> `workflows/03-ba-sprint-batch.md` -> Unify Stages `05 + 08 + 09` into a 2-pass sprint workflow emitting `02-sprints/<SprintID>/FEATURE-XXX.md` in Wave-chunked batches (`3–5` features/pass), then execute `npm run hub:verify -- --hub=<hubDir> --sprint=<SprintID> --strict` and `npm run hub:seal -- --hub=<hubDir> --sprint=<SprintID> --strict` to lock `feature_srd` digests in `SPRINT_<ID>_MANIFEST.md`.
- `@ba-evolve [TargetVersion]` -> `workflows/04-ba-evolve-delta.md` -> Apply post-`v1.0.0` updates *in-place*, append `WAS | CURRENT` Section 10/15 rows, re-seal affected sprint (`npm run hub:seal`), compile delta + optional snapshot (`npm run hub:delta -- --hub=<hubDir> --from=<vPrev> --to=<TargetVersion> --snapshot`), and refresh exports (`npm run hub:export -- --hub=<hubDir>`).
- `@ba-audit [SprintID|ALL]` -> `workflows/05-ba-cross-audit.md` -> Execute `npm run hub:verify -- --hub=<hubDir> --strict` + 6-gate Zero-Gap semantic audit (`STD-08-ZERO-GAP-v2.0`) + `npm run hub:export -- --hub=<hubDir>`.
- `PMTool Sync` -> `npm run hub:pmtool -- --hub=<hubDir> --template=<backlog-import-template.xlsx> --wave=auto [--delta=<vX.Y.Z>]` -> Enforces the 5-level WBS (`CMP-* -> EPC-* -> FEATURE-* -> STR-* -> TSK-*` + `Release` & `Sprint` in `01-roadmap-and-pm/BACKLOG_WBS.md` and Feature Sub-table `1B`), harvests live DB IDs from hidden Columns `Y..AG`, and writes validated wave `.xlsx` imports without touching `Y..AG` or `<dataValidations>`.

## 2. Wave-Chunked Anti-Truncation & Approval Acceleration Rules
1. **Wave-Chunked Anti-Truncation Law:** Never generate >5 features in a single turn or emit generic `«Field»` / `[TBD]` / `{{token}}` mail-merge ACs. Write deep `FEATURE-XXX.md` specs in `Wave 1 -> Wave 2 -> Wave 3` batches of **max `3–5` features per pass**, preserving 100% of screen elements (`Field / Counter / Badge / Filter / CTA`), derived formulas, and concrete `Given / When / Then` ACs.
2. **Approval Acceleration Rule:** Every Pass 1 Question Gate MUST consolidate sprint/kickoff questions into a single numbered table with a concrete **`Option A (Recommended Default)`** per row so the BA can reply **`APPROVE ALL`** or override specific question IDs.

## 3. Zero-Bloat Canonical State & Structured Evolution (`WAS | CURRENT`)
1. **Single Clean Canonical State:** Pre-baseline drafts (`v0.1..v0.9`) edit sections *in-place* until `v1.0.0` is sealed. Never stack `v3.x / v4.x / v5.x Addenda`, stale `NOT_SPEC_SEALED` banners, or `.~lock.*` files inside active hubs.
2. **Post-`v1.0.0` Evolution:** Edit active rules in-place, bump semantic version (`v1.1.0`, `v2.0.0`), append one row to Section 10 / Section 15 (`Ver | Date | Ref | Target ID | WAS | CURRENT | UPDATE NEEDED BY TEAM [BA, PM, Dev, Mobile, QA]`), recompute only affected `feature_srd` digests (`npm run hub:seal`), and emit `03-version-deltas/DELTA_v<From>_to_v<To>.md` (`npm run hub:delta`).

## 4. Screen Decomposition, Seed Defaults & Two-Gate Boundary
1. **Screen Decomposition & Seeds:** Decompose every screen (`M01..MXX`, `A01..AXX`, Figma/PDF) into fields, counters, badges, filters, CTAs, and `6` lifecycle states (`Loading / Empty / Single-Item / Populated / Disabled / Error`). Bind every numeric limit/timer/toggle to a concrete `SEED-*` default in `SEED_DEFAULTS_CATALOG.md` (zero *"unconfigured fail-closed"* punts).
2. **Two-Gate Isolation:** Gate A (`READY_FOR_DEV`: `BA-01..BA-14` with `VALID = 100.0%`, Sections 1–10) is pure BA business truth; Gate B (`READY_TO_CODE`: `ENG-01..ENG-10`, Section 11) is reserved strictly (`PENDING_ENG_AUDIT`) for Engineering (`Backend/Web .ai` & `Mobile 02-FLUTTER ENGINE`).
